    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2034180570683740427",
      "url": "https://x.com/sciencekonek/status/2034180570683740427",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/sciencekonek/status/2034180570683740427",
      "text": "𝟯𝟬𝗧𝗛 𝗔𝗡𝗡𝗜𝗩𝗘𝗥𝗦𝗔𝗥𝗬 𝗢𝗙 𝗧𝗛𝗘 𝗢𝗭𝗢𝗡𝗘 𝗗𝗜𝗦𝗖𝗢 𝗙𝗜𝗥𝗘 🔥\n\nOn this day in 1996, more than 160 lives, mostly graduating students for year-end celebrations, were tragically lost in a fire at Ozone Disco in Quezon City. This is considered the 𝘄𝗼𝗿𝘀𝘁 𝗳𝗶𝗿𝗲 𝗶𝗻 𝗺𝗼𝗱𝗲𝗿𝗻 𝗣𝗵𝗶𝗹𝗶𝗽𝗽𝗶𝗻𝗲 𝗵𝗶𝘀𝘁𝗼𝗿𝘆 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗼𝗻𝗲 𝗼𝗳 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝘄𝗼𝗿𝗹𝗱’𝘀 𝘄𝗼𝗿𝘀𝘁 𝗻𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝗰𝗹𝘂𝗯 𝗱𝗶𝘀𝗮𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗿𝘀.\n\nThe blaze ignited just before midnight, trapping over 300 young patrons and staff inside an overcrowded space. What began as sparks and smoke, mistaken for part of the show, quickly turned into darkness and flames, as blocked exits and locked doors funneled people into a single, fatal choke point.\n\nThe tragedy, which occurred during #FirePreventionMonth, exposed a chain of critical failures: inadequate fire safety systems, the absence of proper emergency exits, severe overcrowding, and the deadly consequences of panic.",
